    "possible_composition": "Keep proven group128 U8B128 and original BF16 FC/Attention. Async packed byte staging remains, but decode directly into the four BF16 A registers immediately consumed by each MMA; preload the two row scales per thread perK128. Remove decoded shared tile and its barrier. Use pinned Marlin U8B128 FP32 bias construction then exact FP32 high-half extraction to BF16 pair and one BF16x2 scaled product. Same ascending MMA K16 and BF16 weight publication. This changes producer/consumer ownership rather than tile size, quantizer or cache tuning.",
